meta {
  name: Update academic session
  type: http
  seq: 10
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/academic-sessions/{{sessionId}}
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "2026-27 (revised)",
    "code": "RENAMED",
    "status": "active"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.name: eq 2026-27 (revised)
  res.body.code: eq 2026-27
  res.body.is_current: eq true
}

docs {
  The trap: code is accepted by the decoder and then never applied. Sessions,
  branches, grade levels and subjects all behave this way, because code is the
  handle timetables and report cards are printed against and a school that
  renames it mid-year breaks everything downstream. Sending a new code is not
  an error and not a change either, so the assert above is what tells you the
  day that stops being true.

  Note also what is NOT sent: is_current. Setting it true here would demote
  every other session, which is right when a year rolls over and wrong as a
  side effect of a rename.
}
